# Normalise line endings on checkin.
#
# This is not cosmetic. Gold tables carry committed content hashes, and the
# `data-contract` CI job re-derives them on both ubuntu and windows runners.
# Without this, a CRLF checkout changes the bytes of every text input and the
# checksums flap between platforms -- a failure that looks like data corruption
# and is actually git.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artifacts: never touch these.
*.parquet binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.tar.xz binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated -- collapse in PR diffs so review stays on the source of truth.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
uv.lock          linguist-generated=true -diff
data/parity/*.json linguist-generated=true -diff
